Filling out forms is one of the most common tasks in web automation and testing. When using Playwright, you have two primary methods for entering text into input fields: .fill() and .pressSequentially(). While both accomplish the same basic goal, choosing the right method can significantly impact the stability, realism, and effectiveness of your tests. locator.fill()
For most scenarios, locator.fill() should be your go-to method. It's fast, efficient, and simulates what happens when a user pastes text into a field. When to use fill(): Simple text inputs without dynamic behavior When you need to quickly populate form fields For basic form submissions where typing simulation isn't critical
